<section class="phero"><div class="phero-media"><img class="phero-img" src="/assets/img/photos/consultation.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/consultation-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/consultation.webp 960w" sizes="100vw" width="960" height="640" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.18"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><a href="/ct-claim-tools/">Claim tools</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><span aria-current="page">Appraisal Readiness Checkup</span></nav><p class="kicker kicker-light">Free checklist</p><h1>Appraisal Readiness Checkup</h1><p class="phero-lede">Strong appraisals are built before the demand letter goes out. Answer twelve questions to see how complete your file is and what to fix first.</p></div></section>
<section class="sec sec-tool"><div class="wrap"><div class="rv">
<div class="tool tool-wide" data-tool="ready">
  <div class="tool-head"><span class="tool-t">Appraisal readiness checkup</span><i>12 questions · about two minutes</i></div>
  <div class="tool-body">
    <div class="tool-in">
      <ol class="quiz"><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get written confirmation that coverage is accepted. If the claim was denied, talk to a Connecticut attorney before considering appraisal."><span>Has the insurer accepted coverage for at least part of the loss?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Ask in writing for the full itemized estimate, not just the payment summary."><span>Do you have the carrier’s complete, line-item estimate?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get an independent line-item estimate. A one-line lump-sum bid won’t hold up in front of a panel."><span>Do you have your own itemized estimate from a contractor or estimator?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Collect every photo and note when each was taken. Add new photos of current conditions."><span>Do you have dated photos taken soon after the loss?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Look in the policy conditions for the paragraph titled “Appraisal” and note any time limits."><span>Have you found and read the appraisal clause in your policy?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Find the “Suit Against Us” condition and put the date on your calendar. Our claim calendar builder can help."><span>Do you know your policy’s suit-limitation period?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Tarp, dry out or board up as needed and keep every invoice."><span>Were temporary repairs made, with receipts saved?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Download it from your insurer’s portal or ask your agent."><span>Do you have your current declarations page?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Make sure attics, wall cavities, subfloors and decking have been checked so the scope is complete."><span>Has hidden damage been opened up and documented?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Gather letters, emails and claim notes in date order."><span>Is your correspondence with the carrier organized by date?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Run the claim gap & fee estimator. A small gap may not justify appraisal costs."><span>Is the gap more than about 10% or several thousand dollars?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Submit any requested proof of loss before the deadline in the carrier’s letter."><span>If a sworn proof of loss was requested, was it submitted on time?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li>
      </ol>
      <div class="btn-row"><button type="button" class="btn line small" data-reset>Reset answers</button></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-out tool-out-gauge" aria-live="polite">
      <div>
        <svg class="gauge" viewBox="0 0 200 110" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 100 A80 80 0 0 1 180 100" fill="none" stroke="#e3eafb" stroke-width="18"/><path data-o="arc" d="M20 100 A80 80 0 0 1 180 100" fill="none" stroke="#1F64E5" stroke-width="18" stroke-dasharray="251.3" stroke-dashoffset="251.3" style="transition:stroke-dashoffset .5s,stroke .3s"/></svg>
        <div class="gauge-num"><span data-o="score">–</span></div>
        <p class="hint center">Answered <span data-o="count">0 / 12</span></p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="out-msg" data-o="verdict"></p>
        <p class="todo-h">Your to-do list</p>
        <ul data-o="todo" class="todo"></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></div>
<p class="hint tool-disc">For planning only. Results depend on the figures you enter and your policy’s terms. They are not a quote, an appraisal or legal advice.</p></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose">
<h2>How the score is weighted</h2>
<p>Questions about coverage, estimates and evidence count most, because they decide whether appraisal is the right tool and how well your number will hold. Administrative items matter too, but they’re easier to fix.</p>
<h2>Reading your result</h2>
<ul><li><strong>75 and above:</strong> a solid file. A professional review of the gap is the logical next step.</li>
<li><strong>45 to 74:</strong> close the open items first. Each one strengthens your position.</li>
<li><strong>Below 45:</strong> demanding appraisal now risks locking in a low number. Build the file first.</li></ul>

<h2>Questions about this tool</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Is anything saved or sent?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No. The checkup runs entirely in your browser and nothing is stored.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can I bring my result to a consultation?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. A screenshot of the to-do list is a helpful starting point.</p></div></details></div>
